y","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Sicily","c":3},{"y":917,"t":"vassal_start","x":"917: Fez accepts Fatimid suzerainty.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":921,"t":"vassal_end","x":"921: the Idrisid Yahya IV of Fez is deposed ('before deposing him in 919'; 921 is the alternative date) and Musa ibn Abul 'Afiya takes charge for the Fatimids.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":2},{"y":921,"t":"gain","x":"921: Fez and Sijilmasa are captured.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":2},{"y":921,"t":"capital_move","x":"921: the capital moves from Raqqada to the new coastal city of Mahdia.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":3},{"y":925,"t":"contest_start","x":"925: the Idrisid Hasan al-Hajam seizes Fez.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":927,"t":"contest_end","x":"927: Musa retakes Fez for the Fatimids.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":931,"t":"loss","x":"931: Musa ibn Abul 'Afiya takes the west over to Cordoba.","cp":"emirate-of-cordoba","cpn":"Emirate of Córdoba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":933,"t":"gain","x":"933: Humayd ibn Yasal defeats Musa.","cp":"emirate-of-cordoba","cpn":"Emirate of Córdoba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":2},{"y":938,"t":"vassal_start","x":"938: the Rif becomes a Fatimid client under the Gannunid Idrisids.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":948,"t":"vassal_end","x":"948: the Gannunids go over to Cordoba.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":948,"t":"capital_move","x":"948: the capital moves to al-Mansuriya near Kairouan.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":3},{"y":948,"t":"vassal_start","x":"948: Sicily becomes a Kalbid client.","cp":"emirate-of-sicily","cpn":"Emirate of Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Sicily","c":3},{"y":948,"t":"loss","x":"948: Cordoba takes the rest of Morocco.","cp":"caliphate-of-cordoba","cpn":"Caliphate of Córdoba","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":2},{"y":958,"t":"vassal_start","x":"958: Jawhar restores Fatimid overlordship over the Idrisids of the Rif.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":969,"t":"vassal_start","x":"969: Mecca and Medina recognise al-Mu'izz.","cp":"Sharifate of Mecca","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_conquest_of_Egypt","c":2},{"y":969,"t":"gain","x":"969: Jawhar takes Fustat and Egypt.","m":7,"cp":"ikhshidid-dynasty","cpn":"Ikhshidid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_conquest_of_Egypt","c":3},{"y":970,"t":"gain","x":"970: Syria falls to the Fatimids.","m":11,"cp":"ikhshidid-dynasty","cpn":"Ikhshidid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_conquest_of_Egypt","c":3},{"y":971,"t":"contest_start","x":"971: the Qarmatians take Damascus and march on Egypt.","m":8,"cp":"qarmatians","cpn":"Qarmatians","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Hasan_al-A%27sam","c":3},{"y":971,"t":"contest_start","x":"971: the Qarmatians invade the Delta.","m":9,"cp":"qarmatians","cpn":"Qarmatians","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_conquest_of_Egypt","c":3},{"y":971,"t":"contest_end","x":"971: the first Qarmatian invasion is beaten in 'two fierce battles on 22 and 24 December 971' at Ayn Shams.","m":12,"cp":"qarmatians","cpn":"Qarmatians","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_conquest_of_Egypt","c":3},{"y":972,"t":"gain","x":"972: Ramla is retaken.","m":5,"cp":"qarmatians","cpn":"Qarmatians","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":3},{"y":972,"t":"vassal_start","x":"972: Buluggin ibn Ziri becomes viceroy of Ifriqiya.","m":10,"cp":"zirid-dynasty","cpn":"Zirid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zirid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":973,"t":"capital_move","x":"973: the caliphate's centre moves to Cairo.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":3},{"y":974,"t":"vassal_end","x":"974: Cordoba retakes the Idrisid lands.","cp":"idrisids","cpn":"Idrisid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":974,"t":"contest_start","x":"974: the second Qarmatian invasion of Egypt.","m":4,"cp":"qarmatians","cpn":"Qarmatians","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Hasan_al-A%27sam","c":3},{"y":974,"t":"contest_end","x":"974: the Qarmatians are beaten.","m":4,"cp":"qarmatians","cpn":"Qarmatians","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Hasan_al-A%27sam","c":3},{"y":975,"t":"contest_start","x":"975: John Tzimiskes campaigns in Syria and Palestine.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I_Tzimiskes","c":2},{"y":976,"t":"contest_end","x":"976: the campaign ends with Tzimiskes' death.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I_Tzimiskes","c":2},{"y":978,"t":"vassal_start","x":"978: Tripolitania goes under Zirid overlordship.","cp":"zirid-dynasty","cpn":"Zirid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zirid_dynasty","c":3},{"y":978,"t":"contest_end","x":"978: the Qarmatians leave Palestine.","cp":"qarmatians","cpn":"Qarmatians","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Hasan_al-A%27sam","c":3},{"y":978,"t":"gain","x":"978: Palestine returns to the Fatimids as the Qarmatians withdraw; the page does not say which towns.","cp":"qarmatians","cpn":"Qarmatians","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Hasan_al-A%27sam","c":2},{"y":983,"t":"gain","x":"983: Damascus is secured.","cp":"local rulers of Damascus (page silent)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":3},{"y":995,"t":"loss","x":"995: the Byzantines garrison Tartus.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basil_II","c":2},{"y":1001,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1001: Tripolitania breaks away.","cp":"zirid-dynasty","cpn":"Zirid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zirid_dynasty","c":2},{"y":1028,"t":"gain","x":"1028: Tartus returns.","cp":"byzantine-empire","cpn":"Byzantine Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basil_II","c":1},{"y":1044,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1044: Sicily's Fatimid tie lapses.","cp":"emirate-of-sicily","cpn":"Emirate of Sicily","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Sicily","c":1},{"y":1048,"t":"vassal_start","x":"1048: the Fatimid da'i Ali al-Sulayhi takes San'a.","cp":"sulayhid-dynasty","cpn":"Sulayhid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":2},{"y":1048,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1048: the Zirids renounce the Fatimids.","cp":"zirid-dynasty","cpn":"Zirid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zirid_dynasty","c":2},{"y":1073,"t":"loss","x":"1073: Atsiz takes Jerusalem.","cp":"great-seljuk-empire","cpn":"Great Seljuk Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":2},{"y":1076,"t":"loss","x":"1076: Atsiz takes Damascus (see 1073).","cp":"great-seljuk-empire","cpn":"Great Seljuk Empire","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":2},{"y":1089,"t":"gain","x":"1089: Badr secures the coast.","cp":"local rulers of the Levantine coast (page silent)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":2},{"y":1098,"t":"gain","x":"1098: al-Afdal retakes Jerusalem.","m":8,"cp":"Artuqids","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":3},{"y":1099,"t":"loss","x":"1099: the crusaders take Jerusalem.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-jerusalem","cpn":"Kingdom of Jerusalem","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem","c":3},{"y":1099,"t":"contest_start","x":"1099: the coastal plain becomes a war zone.","m":7,"cp":"kingdom-of-jerusalem","cpn":"Kingdom of Jerusalem","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem","c":2},{"y":1104,"t":"loss","x":"1104: Raymond of Toulouse takes Byblos (Jubayl).","m":4,"cp":"county-of-tripoli","cpn":"County of Tripoli","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banu_Ammar","c":2},{"y":1110,"t":"loss","x":"1110: Sidon falls to Baldwin I.","m":12,"cp":"kingdom-of-jerusalem","cpn":"Kingdom of Jerusalem","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Sidon_(1110)","c":3},{"y":1124,"t":"loss","x":"1124: Tyre falls.","cp":"kingdom-of-jerusalem","cpn":"Kingdom of Jerusalem","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem","c":2},{"y":1138,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1138: the Yemeni tie ends with the Sulayhid dynasty.","cp":"sulayhid-dynasty","cpn":"Sulayhid dynasty","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulayhid_dynasty","c":2},{"y":1153,"t":"loss","x":"1153: Ascalon falls.","cp":"kingdom-of-jerusalem","cpn":"Kingdom of Jerusalem","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem","c":2},{"y":1153,"t":"contest_end","x":"1153: the fighting over the coastal plain ends with the fall of Ascalon.","cp":"kingdom-of-jerusalem","cpn":"Kingdom of Jerusalem","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem","c":2},{"y":1171,"t":"vassal_end","x":"1171: the Hejaz tie ends with the caliphate.","m":9,"cp":"Sharifate of Mecca","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":1},{"y":1171,"t":"dissolve","x":"1171: Saladin abolishes the Fatimid caliphate.","m":9,"cp":"ayyubid-sultanate","cpn":"Ayyubid Sultanate","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","c":3}],"wars":[{"name":"Sicilian revolt against the Fatimids","from":912,"to":917,"outcome":"The first governor was expelled in 912; Ibn Qurhub rebelled until 916; Palermo surrendered in 917 and Fatimid authority was made secure.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Sicily"},{"name":"Fatimid campaigns in Morocco","from":917,"to":974,"outcome":"Fez suzerain 917, captured 921, lost 925, retaken 927, lost to Cordoba 931 and regained 933; the Gannunids held the north for the Fatimids 938-948; Cordoba took it in 948-954; Jawhar restored overlordship from 958; Ghalib retook it in 973-974.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty"},{"name":"Fatimid conquest of Egypt","from":969,"to":969,"outcome":"Jawhar left Raqqada on 6 February 969, took Fustat on 6 July and had the sermon read in al-Mu'izz's name on 9 July; al-Mu'izz arrived in 973.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_conquest_of_Egypt"},{"name":"Fatimid-Qarmatian wars","from":968,"to":978,"outcome":"Fatimid rule in Syria collapsed in August 1971; two Qarmatian invasions of Egypt were beaten in two battles on 22 and 24 December 971 (at Ayn Shams, per the Conquest of Egypt page) and at Jubb Umayra on 27 April 974; al-A'sam died in March 977; in 978 al-Aziz…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Hasan_al-A%27sam"},{"name":"Fatimid-Byzantine struggle for Syria","from":975,"to":1038,"outcome":"975: the Byzantines retook most of Palestine and Syria, leaving only Tripoli (Fatimid page; the Tzimiskes page lists the towns he took and dates his death 10 January 976: carried as a contest, 975-976); a ten-year truce began in 1001; Fatak occupied Aleppo in…","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate"},{"name":"Zirid break and the Hilalian invasions","from":1048,"to":1057,"outcome":"The Zirids renounced the Fatimid caliphs in 1048-49; the Fatimids sent the Banu Hilal and Banu Sulaym; the Zirids were beaten at Haydaran on 14 April 1052 and left Kairouan for Mahdia in 1057.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zirid_dynasty"},{"name":"Seljuk-aligned Turkmen conquest of Palestine and Damascus","from":1073,"to":1076,"outcome":"Atsiz ibn Uwaq took Jerusalem in 1073 and Damascus in 1076; Badr al-Jamali entered Cairo in January 1074 and rebuilt the army.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate"},{"name":"Crusader-Fatimid wars for the coast","from":1098,"to":1153,"outcome":"Jerusalem retaken August 1098 and lost 15 July 1099; the Egyptian army beaten at Ascalon on 12 August 1099; Byblos lost April 1104 (Banu Ammar page), Sidon 5 December 1110 (Siege of Sidon page; the Kingdom of Jerusalem page says 1111), Tyre 1124, Ascalon 1153.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem"},{"name":"Crusader, Zengid and Byzantine invasions of Egypt","from":1163,"to":1169,"outcome":"Amalric invaded in 1163, besieged Bilbeis with Shirkuh in 1164, was beaten at al-Babein in 1166 and pillaged Bilbeis in 1168; Manuel sent 300 ships in 1169 against Damietta; Shirkuh and then Saladin became viziers in 1169.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem"},{"name":"End of the Fatimid caliphate","from":1169,"to":1171,"outcome":"Saladin, vizier since 26 March 1169, abolished the caliphate after al-Adid's death in September 1171 and had the Abbasid khutba read.","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saladin"}],"certainty":[{"from":909,"to":968,"level":"soft","note":"The Maghreb frontiers (Tahert, Fez, Sijilmasa, the Atlantic edge) are approximate and swing year by year with the Idrisid, Miknasa and Cordoban clients."},{"from":969,"to":1171,"level":"soft","note":"Desert edges of the Nile Valley, the Hejaz and the Syrian marches are approximate; the Crusader-Fatimid coast from 1099 is a series of garrisoned cities (Ascalon, Gaza, Tyre) rather than a line."}],"sources":[{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_Caliphate","title":"Fatimid Caliphate"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fatimid_conquest_of_Egypt","title":"Fatimid conquest of Egypt"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Al-Hasan_al-A%27sam","title":"Al-Hasan al-A'sam"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Zirid_dynasty","title":"Zirid dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kingdom_of_Jerusalem","title":"Kingdom of Jerusalem"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Saladin","title":"Saladin"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emirate_of_Sicily","title":"Emirate of Sicily"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Fatimid_caliphs","title":"List of Fatimid caliphs"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Idrisid_dynasty","title":"Idrisid dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_I_Tzimiskes","title":"John I Tzimiskes"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Basil_II","title":"Basil II"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Sidon_(1110)","title":"Siege of Sidon (1110)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Banu_Ammar","title":"Banu Ammar"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siege_of_Acre_(1104)","title":"Siege of Acre (1104)"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embriaco_family","title":"Embriaco family"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byblos","title":"Byblos"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/County_of_Tripoli","title":"County of Tripoli"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raymond_IV,_Count_of_Toulouse","title":"Raymond IV, Count of Toulouse"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mirdasid_dynasty","title":"Mirdasid dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalbids","title":"Kalbids"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sulayhid_dynasty","title":"Sulayhid dynasty"},{"url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharifate_of_Mecca","title":"Sharifate of Mecca"}]}